This is a toy cli calculator I wrote for learning JIT
compilation. It's written in c, but instead of calculating the result
in c, it compiles the input to machine codes in memory, and then calls
the machine codes.

References:

1. The parser part codes are copied from Bob Nystrom's book - Crafting
Interpreters, it's a wonderful book for learning
compilers. (https://github.com/munificent/craftinginterpreters)

2. I learnt the essence about JIT compilation from Tsoding's
vedio. I also learnt that writing assembly/machine code is eassy - you
just write code in c and feed the c code to
compiler. (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mbFY3Rwv7XM&t=9536s)
